Restoring Database with Different Name

Using RMAN, a database can be restored with different name on same or different name when source DB is available or not available.

Procedure is given below

Add NEW SID entry in oratab file

Get DBID of Source Database
sqlplus rman/*******@rmanprd
SQL> select DBID,NAME from rc_database;

Create password file.
Export ORACLE_SID=<new sid>
cd $ORACLE_HOME/dbs
orapwd file=orapw<new sid> password=p0#ass1um force=yes

export ORA_RMAN_SGA_TARGET 
export ORA_RMAN_SGA_TARGET=500M

Set DBID of Source database and start the database in nomount state
rman target / catalog= rman/*******@rmanprd
RMAN> set dbid <3880765485> ;
RMAN>startup nomount;
Restore SP file in /tmp location
RUN {
ALLOCATE CHANNEL ch001 TYPE 'SBT_TAPE'…..;

RESTORE SPFILE TO '/tmp/spfilePLM2T.ora' for db_unique_name PLM2TLSG;
RELEASE CHANNEL ch001;
}

Shutdown the database
RMAN> shutdown immediate.


Create pfile from the restored spfile
SQL> create pfile='/db/app/oracle/product/11.2.0/dbhome_1/dbs/initplm2tres.ora' from spfile='/tmp/spfilePLM2T.ora';

Edit the Pfile according to new database name (DB_NAME should not be changed)
Check Attached Test case for reference

Restore the Control file
sqlplus / as sysdba
startup nomount
rman target / catalog= rman/*******@rmanprd
RMAN> set DBID=534662516
RUN {
ALLOCATE CHANNEL ch001 TYPE 'SBT_TAPE'…. ;
set until time "to_date('2014-09-06:18:00:00', 'yyyy-mm-dd:hh24:mi:ss')";
RESTORE controlfile;
RELEASE CHANNEL ch001;
}
Change the redo log location according to new db name
sqlplus / as sysdba
alter database mount;
alter database rename file '/db/redolog.001/plm2tlsg/redolog_1.rdo' to '/db-new/arc5qls3.005/oradata/redolog_1.rdo';
Check Attached Test case for reference

Restore the Database (Set New Names to Data files in rman script)
Check Attached Test case for reference

Recover the database as per required Sequence Number or time
run
{
ALLOCATE CHANNEL ch003 TYPE 'SBT_TAPE' …;
set until time "to_date('2014-09-06:18:00:00', 'yyyy-mm-dd:hh24:mi:ss')";
recover database;
}
run
{
ALLOCATE CHANNEL ch003 TYPE 'SBT_TAPE' …;
set until sequence 2334;
recover database;
}
Change DB Name to New DB Name
sqlplus / as sysdba
SQL> alter database backup controlfile to trace;
shut immediate
Edit init<SID>.ora file 
Change Parameter : DB_NAME=NEW SID
sqlplus / as sysdba
SQL> startup nomount
Create New Control file with changed DB name (Get script Form Trace and change the script accordingly)
CREATE CONTROLFILE REUSE SET DATABASE "<NEW DBNAME>" RESETLOGS  ARCHIVELOG…
Open Database using reset logs option
SQL> alter database open resetlogs;
Create Temporary Tablespace
create temporary tablespace TEMP1 tempfile '/db-new/arc5qls3.005/oradata/temp01.dbf' size 1 G;
alter database default temporary tablespace TEMP1;
Drop tablespace TEMP;
